From 6f60b3e7548bcccf562274a58830a323fd1e4c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:32:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: std::shuffle, std::generate and
 std::next_permutation over the range a macro hands them

The emitter lowers an algorithm it has no entry for to an attribute of
ROOT.std, so the three arrive at _Namespace as the range the call gave:
two iterators of one vector, or a pointer and the tail it leaves over. The
algorithms themselves are in cppstd.objects beside sort_range, and take the
container with the span, because C++ writes back through the iterators.
std::default_random_engine is libc++'s minstd_rand0, which shuffle needs.

other/math: mathcore-stressTMath and mathcore-testSampleQuantiles now PASS.
